sentence_before:
Since direct evaluation is costly and task-dependent, we use the auditable editorial-fidelity proxy
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
F_{\mathrm{editorial}}(R)={}&w_sS_{\mathrm{salience}}+w_tS_{\mathrm{state}}+w_aS_{\mathrm{answer}}\\
&+w_pS_{\mathrm{provenance}}+w_lS_{\mathrm{language}}.
\end{aligned}
\label{eq:fidelity}
\end{equation}
where $\sum_jw_j=1$ and $w_j\geq0$.

sentence_after:
Since direct evaluation is costly and task-dependent, we employ the auditable editorial-fidelity proxy
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
F_{\mathrm{editorial}}(R)={}&w_sS_{\mathrm{salience}}+w_tS_{\mathrm{state}}+w_aS_{\mathrm{answer}}\\
&+w_pS_{\mathrm{provenance}}+w_lS_{\mathrm{language}}.
\end{aligned}
\label{eq:fidelity}
\end{equation}
where $\sum_jw_j=1$ and $w_j\geq0$.

sentence_before:
Morphena formulates representation allocation as
\begin{equation}
\min_R C(R)
\quad\text{s.t.}\quad
F_{\mathrm{editorial}}(R)\geq\rho,
\end{equation}
or equivalently,
\begin{equation}
\max_R\left[F_{\mathrm{editorial}}(R)-\lambda C(R)\right],
\qquad \lambda\geq0,
\end{equation}
yielding a cost--fidelity frontier.

