sentence_before:
The temporal coverage component is defined as
\begin{equation}
F(\mathcal{S})=\sum_t a_t\max_{s\in\mathcal{S}}
\exp(-|t-s|/\tau),\qquad a_t\geq0.
\end{equation}
The objective is monotonic submodular, allowing the well-known $(1 - 1/e)$ greedy approach to apply to the cardinality constraint.

sentence_after:
The temporal coverage component is defined as
\begin{equation}
F(\mathcal{S})=\sum_t a_t\max_{s\in\mathcal{S}}
\exp(-|t-s|/\tau),\qquad a_t\geq0.
\end{equation}
The objective is monotonic submodular, permitting the well-known $(1 - 1/e)$ greedy approach to apply to the cardinality constraint.

